== Public Functions ==

=== <code>decide(params, now)</code> ===

Works out the complete state of the box. This is where every judgement is made; <code>render</code> only formats the result.

'''Parameters:'''
* <code>params</code> (table): <code>date</code>, <code>base</code>, <code>force</code> (boolean), <code>pin</code> (boolean), <code>reason</code>, <code>discography</code>, <code>nocat</code>, <code>needrom</code>
* <code>now</code> (table): <code>{ year =, month =, day = }</code>

'''Returns:''' a state table containing <code>tier</code>, <code>label</code>, <code>icon</code>, <code>color</code>, <code>meter</code>, <code>category</code>, <code>months</code>, <code>dated</code>, <code>forced</code>, <code>pinned</code> and the passthrough fields.

'''Precedence''' — these are checked in order, and the first match wins:
# '''Forced''' — <code>force</code> is true, a <code>reason</code> was given, or the date is missing or unparseable. Tier is <code>outdated</code>, colour is flat grey, meter is 3%.
# '''Pinned''' — <code>pin</code> is true and the date parsed. Tier is <code>fresh</code>, the header reads "Marked as completed", the meter is full and the colour does '''not''' fade.
# '''By age''' — <code>classify(months)</code> decides between fresh, aging and outdated.

An explicit outdated flag therefore always beats a pin.

=== <code>render(state, meta_html)</code> ===

Turns a state table into the box markup. <code>meta_html</code> is the pre-expanded footer from [[Module:Freshness]], and may be an empty string.

The description line varies:
* a <code>reason</code>, if one was given
* "Last updated '''date'''. Flagged as outdated." when forced with a date
* "This song list is flagged as outdated." when forced without one
* "Song list last updated '''date'''." otherwise — including when pinned, since the pinned wording lives in the header instead

When <code>discography</code> is set, "song list" in that line is widened to "song list and discography".

=== <code>categories(state)</code> ===

Returns the category wikitext, or an empty string when <code>nocat</code> is set. Uses {{T|ForAllUtaite}} to pick the utaite or youtaite variant, and appends [[:Category:Songlists requiring romanization]] when <code>needrom</code> is set.

The caller must expand this with <code>frame:preprocess</code>; see [[Module:Freshness]].

=== <code>parse_date(s)</code> ===

Returns <code>year, month, day</code>, or <code>nil</code> when nothing matches. Accepted forms:
* <code>2023年10月31日</code>
* <code>2023-10-31</code>, <code>2023/10/31</code>, <code>2023.10.31</code>
* <code>October 31, 2023</code> — month name full or abbreviated, comma and ordinal suffix optional

=== Colour helpers ===

{| class="wikitable"
! Function !! Purpose
|-
| <code>is_hex(s)</code> || True only for exactly 6 hex digits, with or without a leading <code>#</code>
|-
| <code>is_css_color(s)</code> || True for any other CSS colour safe to place in an inline style: short hex, X11 names, <code>var(--x)</code>, <code>rgb()</code>, <code>hsl()</code>. Rejects anything containing <code>;</code> <code>{}</code> <code>&lt;&gt;</code> quotes or a backslash, and anything mentioning <code>expression</code>, <code>javascript</code> or <code>url</code>
|-
| <code>fade(hex, months)</code> || Blends a hex colour toward grey, reaching full grey at <code>FADE_MAX</code>
|-
| <code>mix(css, months)</code> || Emits <code>color-mix(in srgb, …)</code> so the browser performs the same fade for colours Lua cannot resolve to RGB
|-
| <code>hex_to_rgb</code>, <code>rgb_to_hex</code> || Conversion helpers used by <code>fade</code>
|}

Hex is faded in Lua; everything else is faded by the browser. Values that satisfy neither test fall back to <code>BASE_DEFAULT</code>.

=== Other helpers ===

{| class="wikitable"
! Function !! Purpose
|-
| <code>classify(months)</code> || Maps a month count to <code>fresh</code>, <code>aging</code> or <code>outdated</code>
|-
| <code>months_between(y1,m1,d1,y2,m2,d2)</code> || Whole months elapsed, counting a partial month as incomplete
|-
| <code>meter(months)</code> || Progress-bar percentage, floored at 3% so the bar never vanishes
|-
| <code>ago(months)</code> || Human phrasing such as "this month", "5 months ago", "2 years 9 mo ago"
|-
| <code>split_params(body)</code> || Splits a template body into positional and named parameters
|-
| <code>from_subpage_params(text)</code> || Finds a {{T|Outdated}} or {{T|Uptodate}} call in subpage wikitext and returns its parameters, forcing outdated for the former
|}

== Technical Considerations ==

=== Limitations ===
* <code>split_params</code> and <code>from_subpage_params</code> match with a simple pattern and cannot handle a nested <code><nowiki>{{...}}</nowiki></code> inside a parameter value
* <code>from_subpage_params</code> reads only the first recognised call on the page
* <code>mix</code> relies on CSS <code>color-mix()</code>, which needs a browser from 2023 or later; older browsers fall back to the stylesheet default

=== Dependencies ===
None. This module deliberately requires nothing, not even <code>mw</code>.

